From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Johannes Stein <johannesstein@freeze-dev.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 17:34:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 01/78] Register Default() zero symbols immediately (#41929)

handle_default creates the $_zero_$ staticvarsym in the current module's
localsymtable but leaves it unregistered (SymId=-2) until the unit
finishes. Inlining a routine that uses Default(T) into another unit of
the same unit cycle imports the symbol through tmodule.addimportedsym,
which indexes symlist[-2] and raises EListError.
---
 compiler/ninl.pas | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/compiler/ninl.pas b/compiler/ninl.pas
index 85c22f2f..6730dad7 100644
--- a/compiler/ninl.pas
+++ b/compiler/ninl.pas
@@ -534,6 +534,11 @@ implementation
                   tabstractvarsym(srsym).varstate:=vs_initialised;
 
                   srsymtable.insertsym(srsym);
+                  { register it now: when this unit is part of a unit cycle,
+                    another unit can inline a routine whose body loads this
+                    symbol before this unit registers its symbols at the end,
+                    and tmodule.addimportedsym needs a valid SymId (#41929) }
+                  tstoredsym(srsym).register_sym;
                   cnodeutils.insertbssdata(tstaticvarsym(srsym));
                 end;
               result:=cloadnode.create(srsym,srsymtable);
